# Rust
/router/target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# Model caches and training artifacts.
#
# The bge-small ONNX model is ~130MB and is fetched on first run into the cache
# directory shared with zeromem; it is never committed. `weights.json` IS
# committed — it is 384 floats plus a bias, and the router cannot route without
# it — but the intermediate embedding matrices used to fit it are not.
/train/.cache/
/train/embeddings-*.npy
*.onnx

# Runtime state
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
/deploy/.state/

# Secrets. The stack needs exactly one credential (NEURALWATT_API_KEY); it is
# supplied by the environment or a systemd EnvironmentFile, never by a tracked
# file. `.env.example` is tracked and documents the variable names.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# The training set, downloaded by train/fetch_dataset.py. ~50MB, and
# reproducible from a one-line command, so it is fetched rather than tracked.
/train/prompts.jsonl

# The routing core, compiled for iOS. 84 MB of build output, reproducible from
# the Rust beside it by scripts/build-ios-core.sh, and rebuilt on every change to
# the core — a repository carrying it would carry those bytes again each time.
ios/WattRouterFFI.xcframework/
ios/.build/

# The Xcode project, generated from ios/project.yml by `just ios-project`. A
# checked-in pbxproj is unreviewable under this repository's size limit: it is
# generated, it reorders itself between Xcode versions, and it conflicts on every
# parallel change. The spec beside it says the same thing in a file people can read.
ios/WattRouter.xcodeproj/
